# AIROM's own detection knowledge is not AIROM's dependencies.
#
# A scanner's source necessarily contains the names of everything it can find:
# `{"huggingface/text-generation-inference", "tgi"}` in an image table,
# `"@mistralai/mistralai": "mistralai"` in a provider normalization map. Those
# are patterns, not calls. Without this file a self-scan reports that AIROM runs
# Ollama and depends on the Mistral SDK, neither of which is true — AIROM is a
# deterministic Go binary that calls no model (ARCHITECTURE.md: no LLM, no
# network during a scan).
#
# This is a fact about THIS repository, not a rule AIROM applies to yours. The
# same table in a gateway that routes to those providers is a true finding, and
# no static analysis can tell the two apart — so the judgement is recorded here,
# by the only people who know the answer, instead of guessed at in a detector.
#
# Rule packs and lifecycle catalogs need no entry: they are recognised
# structurally (pkg/airom/detect.IsAIROMConfig), which protects your custom
# packs too, not just ours.

# Pattern tables: image names, module paths, provider aliases, env-var keys.
internal/detectors/
internal/source/

# The provider-alias normalization map (§9.1 canonical identity).
internal/assemble/

# The embedded rule packs themselves.
rules/
